{
  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Lab 4 — HeatAlert, WeatherHistory & HeatMail"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "# Lab 4 — `HeatAlert`, `WeatherHistory` & `HeatMail`\n\nIn this lab, you will connect three new pieces to `campus/weather/reading`:\n1. **`HeatAlert` (Action):** Compares `temperature_c` against the retained threshold on `config/heat_limit_c` and uses a retained flag (`campus/weather/alerts/heat_active`) so an alert fires **only once** when a heat wave starts — not on every 60-second poll.\n2. **`WeatherHistory` (CSV Connector):** Appends every reading as a new row in `project/exports/campus-weather.csv`.\n3. **`HeatMail` (Email Connector):** Sends an HTML alert email (using `templates/heat-alert.html`) to Mailpit (`http://localhost:8025`) whenever `campus/weather/alerts/heat` fires.\n\n> **Prerequisite check:** Make sure you published `30` with **Retain ON** to `config/heat_limit_c` in `00-setup`.\n\n### Cell 1: Deploy `HeatAlert`\nNotice how `KEEP TOPIC \"campus/weather/alerts/heat_active\" WITH \"on\"` publishes a **retained** message (`KEEP TOPIC` = `PUBLISH TOPIC` with Retain ON), and `GET TOPIC \"...\"` reads that retained state on the next run.\n\nClick **▷** on each of the 3 cells below (or click **Deploy All** at the top right):"
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "lot",
      "value": "DEFINE ACTION HeatAlert\nON TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading\" DO\n    SET \"temp_c\" WITH (GET JSON \"temperature_c\" IN PAYLOAD AS DOUBLE)\n    SET \"limit\" WITH (GET TOPIC \"config/heat_limit_c\" AS DOUBLE)\n    SET \"active\" WITH (GET TOPIC \"campus/weather/alerts/heat_active\" AS STRING)\n    IF {temp_c} > {limit} THEN\n        IF {active} != \"on\" THEN\n            KEEP TOPIC \"campus/weather/alerts/heat_active\" WITH \"on\"\n            PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/alerts/heat\" WITH PAYLOAD\n    ELSE\n        KEEP TOPIC \"campus/weather/alerts/heat_active\" WITH \"off\"\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "### Cell 2: Deploy `WeatherHistory` (CSV Connector)\nEvery JSON message on `campus/weather/reading` is appended as a row to `/data/exports/campus-weather.csv` (mounted on your computer at `project/exports/campus-weather.csv`).\n\n> **Note:** In the HUB's **Connectors** window, `WeatherHistory` may show a red status indicator until its first message arrives — that is normal for file-based Connectors."
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "lot",
      "value": "DEFINE CONNECTOR WeatherHistory WITH TYPE CSV\n    ADD CSV_CONFIG\n        WITH FILE_PATH \"/data/exports/campus-weather.csv\"\n        WITH DELIMITER \",\"\n        WITH HAS_HEADER TRUE\n        WITH CREATE_IF_MISSING TRUE\n    ADD EVENT AppendReading\n        WITH SOURCE_TOPIC \"campus/weather/reading\"\n        WITH MODE \"APPEND\"\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "### Cell 3: Deploy `HeatMail` (Email Connector)\nWhen `HeatAlert` publishes a reading to `campus/weather/alerts/heat`, `HeatMail` fills the `{value.json.*}` placeholders inside `/templates/heat-alert.html` and sends the email to Mailpit."
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "lot",
      "value": "DEFINE CONNECTOR HeatMail WITH TYPE EMAIL\n    ADD SMTP_CONFIG\n        WITH SERVER (GET ENV \"SMTP_HOST\")\n        WITH PORT 1025\n        WITH USERNAME (GET ENV \"SMTP_USER\")\n        WITH PASSWORD (GET SECRET \"SMTP_PASSWORD\")\n        WITH USE_TLS FALSE\n    ADD EVENT SendHeatEmail\n        WITH SOURCE_TOPIC \"campus/weather/alerts/heat\"\n        WITH TO \"ops@example.com\"\n        WITH SUBJECT \"Campus heat alert\"\n        WITH TEMPLATE_PATH \"/templates/heat-alert.html\"\n        WITH IS_HTML TRUE\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "### Test the alert and email\n\n1. **Normal reading (`limit = 30`):** In **Data Viewer → Publish**, send `poll` to `campus/weather/request`. Check that `campus/weather/alerts/heat_active` is `\"off\"` and a new row appears in `project/exports/campus-weather.csv`.\n2. **Trigger a heat wave (`limit = 1`):**\n   - Publish `1` with **Retain ON** to `config/heat_limit_c`.\n   - Publish `poll` to `campus/weather/request`.\n   - `campus/weather/alerts/heat_active` flips to `\"on\"` and `campus/weather/alerts/heat` receives the reading.\n   - Open **Mailpit** at [http://localhost:8025](http://localhost:8025) — you should see one **Campus heat alert** email!\n3. **Test deduplication:** Publish `poll` to `campus/weather/request` a second time. Because `heat_active` is already `\"on\"`, **no second email** is sent.\n4. **Reset:** Publish `30` with **Retain ON** to `config/heat_limit_c`, then publish `poll` to `campus/weather/request` (`heat_active` returns to `\"off\"`).\n\n**Next up:** Open **`05-rules.lotnb`** to lock down `config/#` so only `root` can change the threshold."
    }
  ]
}
